"TRACKING_TERMS_TITLE" = "Terms of use for tracking";
"TRACKING_TERMS_TEXT" = "I agree to share my phone's location with others, even if the app on my phone is closed.\
\
The service uses the device's internal GPS to measure distance during a trip. Continuous use of GPS affects battery consumption. If the application only runs in the background, battery consumption is reduced.\
\
The system keeps a location history for three months in order to monitor and investigate customer problems and complaints. In addition, the company is responsible for monthly backups and/or printouts of reports.\
\
The user knows that when GPS is turned off on the device (screen), it is impossible to determine the location of the subscriber.\
\
If an employee is inside a closed building, underground car park, tunnel, etc., this may result in the employee's location being impossible or inaccurate, which may cause measurement deviations.\
\
The employer is responsible for the service and must inform the employee about the service.\
The company is not responsible for device or communication problems. The Client is aware that from time to time there may be problems with communication or transmission of information.\
\
The Service is subject to the Customer Service Agreement, its terms and conditions.\
\
If necessary (vacation, backup service, etc.), the employee can block the determination of his location in the settings menu of his device. In this case, the employee is displayed on the map in red.\
\
The accumulated information depends on the device and the measurements made via the device's GPS. As a result, deviations beyond the control of the company are possible. When measuring distance, the deviation range is taken into account.\
\
The company is not responsible for GPS or satellites and presents the image as received from the device.";
